  "actionableFindingsRemaining": [],
  "sourceReview": [
    "Single foreground animation loop starts before either fetch. Blur, hidden and persisted departure stop sampling and clear edits/input; foreground restoration schedules at most one loop and requires neutral input. Terminal departure destroys owners/listeners.",
    "Current guards after fetch and body completion fence terminal mutations. Persisted pages may finish catalogue DOM updates without restoring focus or polling. This distinction is explicit in tests and documentation.",
    "Real shared SELECT draft signatures invalidate changed options without committing them or stealing usable focus. SUMMARY retains native disclosure behavior. Back cancels edit before page Return and Confirm is separate.",
    "Pending/failing release catalogues preserve current-build fallback and correctly initialized history action. Choosing a build only changes the Open link. No automatic navigation or player-data writes were added.",
    "Strict archived-play validator and generic game release resolver are unchanged. Valid relative records rebase against fetched/requested catalogue URL; canonical HTTPS destinations retain exact identity.",
    "About loads shared focus/theme styling. New local previews use readable theme tokens and complete rows; dedicated page status honors Large secondary text. Source structure is consistent, but actual layout/input/accessibility acceptance is not inferred.",
    "Docs and maintainer prompt describe the implemented contract and preserve existing guidance. They keep modeled, native, physical-device and public qualifications separate."
  ],
